A block X of mass $m_X$ slides in a straight line along a horizontal frictionless surface, as shown in Fig. 3.1.

{{figure:figure_3_1.png}}

{{figure:figure_3_2.png}}

The block X, moving with speed $5v$, collides head-on with a stationary block Y of mass $m_Y$. The two blocks stick together and then move with common speed $v$, as shown in Fig. 3.2.

The variation with time $t$ of the momentum of block X in (b) is shown in Fig. 3.3.

{{figure:figure_3_3.png}}

Block X makes contact with block Y at time $t = 20\text{ ms}$.
